2e3e15c7-3c34-4960-99fe-309285bfaf6b	0dbd3623-73fe-4d9c-a316-206b751cc872	Claudio Fiordellisi, also known as Fiore, received his first camera (pictured below) when he was six years old from his father. At the time, Fiore lived in Milano, Italy, where he grew up and became a professional photographer. As supervisor in one of the largest commercial photography labs in Milano, to freelance photographer for advertisements, portraits, and weddings, Fiore continued his on-going love and career in photography when he moved to the United States to be with his future wife. Fiore's agility, love of travel, and attention to detail complement his work as a visual artist. Fiore's interest and subsequent education in film-making guide his latest work. With a Bachelor degree from the Institute of American Indian Arts in Cinematic Art and Technology with high honors, he broadened his abilities by working with the latest in camera digital technology equipment and software. As a photographer he works individually and in film he works collaboratively as part of a team. Still, his contributions in either medium remain the same: an artist that can see things that others may quickly dismiss, his original eye and unique perspective, and the way a scene is successfully composed. Currently, he lives in Santa Fe, New Mexico.	\N	[]	1	\N	\N	\N	10	0	{English}	\N	25	{}	t	f	0.00	0	\N	0.00	f	1	\N	2025-10-13 22:27:35.197+00	2025-10-13 22:27:34.976986+00	\N	\N	\N	0	0	f	\N	\N	\N	female	{Modern}	t	f	{}	\N	Memphis	LA	38111	USA	f	{}	f	f	f	f	f	t	f	t
7a593584-89b8-4d1e-a5b1-4512630af0da	64875a8d-f9ce-447a-85d2-f7339889e096	Tulips are elegant, colorful flowers that have long symbolized love, happiness, and the beauty of spring. Originally from Central Asia, they became famous in the Netherlands during the 17th century’s “Tulip Mania,” when their popularity made them a symbol of wealth and desire. Today, tulips are cherished around the world for their bright, cup-shaped blooms and come in countless varieties and colors, each carrying a different meaning. Red tulips often represent true love, while yellow ones symbolize cheerfulness and friendship. Blooming in early to late spring, tulips thrive in cool climates and well-drained soil. Their simple yet striking form makes them a favorite in gardens, floral arrangements, and festivals alike. Whether planted in clusters or given as a gift, tulips capture the essence of renewal and optimism that spring brings each year.\n	\N	[]	1	\N	\N	\N	18	0	{English}	\N	25	{}	t	f	0.00	0	\N	0.00	f	1	\N	2025-10-13 22:33:23.176+00	2025-10-13 22:33:23.268458+00	\N	\N	\N	0	0	f	\N	\N	\N	male	{"Documentary Style"}	t	f	{}	\N	Sacramento	CA	95825	USA	f	{}	t	t	t	f	f	t	f	t
