aeba4eb2-ad7b-4901-9b43-6d09a20df78d	71291f08-9440-4450-9fe0-4e0d9af16112	Tulips are elegant, colorful flowers that have long symbolized love, happiness, and the beauty of spring. Originally from Central Asia, they became famous in the Netherlands during the 17th century’s “Tulip Mania,” when their popularity made them a symbol of wealth and desire. Today, tulips are cherished around the world for their bright, cup-shaped blooms and come in countless varieties and colors, each carrying a different meaning. Red tulips often represent true love, while yellow ones symbolize cheerfulness and friendship. Blooming in early to late spring, tulips thrive in cool climates and well-drained soil. Their simple yet striking form makes them a favorite in gardens, floral arrangements, and festivals alike. Whether planted in clusters or given as a gift, tulips capture the essence of renewal and optimism that spring brings each year.	\N	[]	1	\N	\N	\N	0	0	{English}	\N	25	{}	f	f	0.00	0	\N	0.00	f	1	\N	2025-10-16 03:19:09.281+00	2025-10-16 03:19:09.320233+00	\N	\N	\N	0	0	f	\N	\N	\N	\N	{}	f	f	{https://ldxscjxoakqrmkgqwwhr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/photographer-portfolios/71291f08-9440-4450-9fe0-4e0d9af16112/1760581140131-c2zj9ru8w.jpg,https://ldxscjxoakqrmkgqwwhr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/photographer-portfolios/71291f08-9440-4450-9fe0-4e0d9af16112/1760581140132-1f27m1mph.jpg,https://ldxscjxoakqrmkgqwwhr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/photographer-portfolios/71291f08-9440-4450-9fe0-4e0d9af16112/1760581140132-qa0a6oiby.jpg,https://ldxscjxoakqrmkgqwwhr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/photographer-portfolios/71291f08-9440-4450-9fe0-4e0d9af16112/1760581140132-yw925lsih.jpg,https://ldxscjxoakqrmkgqwwhr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/photographer-portfolios/71291f08-9440-4450-9fe0-4e0d9af16112/1760581140132-t6j8pfsew.jpg,https://ldxscjxoakqrmkgqwwhr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/photographer-portfolios/71291f08-9440-4450-9fe0-4e0d9af16112/176058114